# Walkthrough - HTTPS & Mixed Content Fixes

I have implemented the necessary changes to fix the **Mixed Content** errors and insure correct **HTTPS redirection** across your microservices.

## Changes Made

### 1. API Gateway Middleware
I added a custom middleware to `services/api-gateway/main.py` that explicitly trusts the `X-Forwarded-Proto` header. This ensures that even behind a proxy (Cloudflare/Kubernetes Ingress), FastAPI knows the original request was `https`.

```python
@app.middleware("http")
async def forward_proto_middleware(request: Request, call_next):
    if request.headers.get("x-forwarded-proto") == "https":
        request.scope["scheme"] = "https"
    return await call_next(request)
```

### 2. Dockerfile Updates (All Services)
I updated the `CMD` for **all 9 microservices** to include the `--proxy-headers` flag and allow forwarded IPs from the proxy.

**Modified Dockerfiles:**
- [x] `api-gateway/Dockerfile`
- [x] `auth-service/Dockerfile`
- [x] `user-service/Dockerfile`
- [x] `product-service/Dockerfile`
- [x] `cart-service/Dockerfile`
- [x] `order-service/Dockerfile`
- [x] `payment-service/Dockerfile`
- [x] `review-service/Dockerfile`
- [x] `wishlist-service/Dockerfile`

**Updated Command:**
```dockerfile
CMD ["uvicorn", "main:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8000", "--proxy-headers", "--forwarded-allow-ips='*'"]
```

## How to Deploy These Changes

Since these changes are in the `Dockerfile` and source code, you need to rebuild and push the images:

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Run these commands from your terminal to update the cluster:

```bash
# 1. Build and push all services (You can do this for each service you modified)
cd services/api-gateway && docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64 -t aksacr.azurecr.io/api-gateway:v1 --push .
cd ../auth-service && docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64 -t aksacr.azurecr.io/auth-service:v1 --push .
# ... repeat for other services if needed ...

# 2. Restart the pods to pull the new images
kubectl rollout restart deployment stream-api-deploy
kubectl rollout restart deployment auth-service-ecomm
```

## Verification
Once deployed, you can verify the fix by running:
`curl -I -H "X-Forwarded-Proto: https" https://api.puneetdevops.online/auth`

The `Location` header should now correctly show `https://api.puneetdevops.online/auth/` (instead of `http`).
